# Shared Library Management Guide

## Architecture

This workspace uses a **Shared Library** pattern:
- `.shared/` contains all reusable components (scripts, skills, rules, commands)
- Each Knowledge Space gets transparent access via NTFS junctions (directories) and hard links (files)
- `bridge.ps1` manages all connections

## When You Add a New Shared Component

### Adding a new `.mdc` rule file

1. Create the file in `.shared/cursor-rules/your-rule.mdc`
2. Run `.\bridge.ps1 sync-shared` — auto-discovers new `.mdc` files and creates hard links in all spaces
3. Done. No manual edits to `bridge.ps1` needed (hardlinks are auto-discovered from `.shared/cursor-rules/*.mdc`)

### Adding a new shared directory (junction)

1. Create the directory in `.shared/your-directory/`
2. Edit `bridge.ps1` — add entry to `$JunctionDefs`:
   ```powershell
   @{ Local = "your-local-path"; Target = "$SharedDir\your-directory" }
   ```
3. Run `.\bridge.ps1 sync-shared` to propagate to all spaces

### Adding a new shared file (non-.mdc)

1. Place the file in the appropriate `.shared/` subdirectory
2. If it's inside a junction-linked directory (scripts/, claude-skills/, claude-commands/), it's automatically available
3. If it needs its own hard link, add to `Get-SharedHardlinkDefs` function in `bridge.ps1`

## Key Commands

| Command | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.\bridge.ps1 sync-shared` | Auto-discover new shared components, propagate to all spaces, update .space.json |
| `.\bridge.ps1 verify` | Check all links are healthy across all spaces |
| `.\bridge.ps1 repair` | Fix broken links (re-runs setup on all spaces) |
| `.\bridge.ps1 add-space "Name"` | Create a new Knowledge Space with all shared links |
| `.\bridge.ps1 status` | Overview of all spaces and shared component counts |

## Important: Auto-Discovery

`bridge.ps1` uses `Get-SharedHardlinkDefs` to dynamically scan `.shared/cursor-rules/*.mdc`.
This means:
- **New `.mdc` files** in `.shared/cursor-rules/` are auto-detected — just run `sync-shared`
- **Removed `.mdc` files** will show as orphan hard links — manually delete from spaces or ignore
- **Junction definitions** are static in `$JunctionDefs` — must be manually added/removed

## Space Independence

Each Knowledge Space can be opened independently as a separate workspace. Junctions use absolute paths
and resolve correctly regardless of the current working directory. When opening a single space:
- Shared scripts, skills, commands are accessible via junctions
- Shared cursor rules are accessible via hard links
- Space-specific content (purpose.md, schema.md, CLAUDE.md, wiki/) stays local
